<article class="env-lemma" id="0FAJ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FAJ">Lemma <span data-tag="0FAJ">42.47.6</span>.</a> In Lemma <a href="/tag/0F9H" data-tag="0F9H">42.47.1</a> let $f : Y \to X$ be locally of finite type and say $c \in A^*(Y \to X)$. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  c \circ P'_ p(E_2) = P'_ p(Lf_2^*E_2) \circ c \quad \text{resp.}\quad c \circ c'_ p(E_2) = c'_ p(Lf_2^*E_2) \circ c  \]
</div>
  <p> in $A^*(Y_2 \to Y)$ where $f_2 : Y_2 \to X_2$ is the base change of $f$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\alpha \in \mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits _ k(X)$. We may write 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \alpha = \alpha _1 + \alpha _2  \]
</div>
    <p>
       with $\alpha _ i \in \mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits _ k(X_ i)$; we are omitting the pushforwards by the closed immersions $X_ i \to X$. The reader then checks that $c'_ p(E_2) \cap \alpha = c_ p(E_2) \cap \alpha _2$, $c \cap c'_ p(E_2) \cap \alpha = c \cap c_ p(E_2) \cap \alpha _2$, $c \cap \alpha = c \cap \alpha _1 + c \cap \alpha _2$, and $c'_ p(Lf_2^*E_2) \cap c \cap \alpha = c_ p(Lf_2^*E_2) \cap c \cap \alpha _2$. We conclude by Lemma <a href="/tag/0FAC" data-tag="0FAC">42.46.6</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>